**SHIP (code) — with the runtime evidence gate explicitly still open.**

**Code verdict.** I reviewed all listed files plus the interfaces they depend on (troika 0.52.5 anchoring, codec, TTF binary). The registration math is exact: normalized glyphs place the black-box min at the local origin, `fontMinX/fontMinY/fontHeight` are real fontTools bounds (TTF head verified UPM 1000), and the rotated offset in sheetText.ts provably reproduces handwrite's placed bounds for any rotation (troika `anchorX:'left'`/`top-baseline` leave the pen origin at the member position; the AABB terms cancel). Letters are one SDF member each in the existing BatchedText with group/key/dur clip reveal; contours never enter ink.path (test-pinned); circles/leaders/strikes stay vector ink; cache version 8 rides the container header and texts round-trip verbatim through the sidecar (regeneration log `"exact": true`). Static gates are green: typecheck, 41 files/435 tests, build, Station2, B1/B2. Punctuation `.` `!` `-` (and `9`) fall back to legacy vector strokes; that's recorded in final-verification.json and invisible at reading size — consistent with the accepted look, not retuned.

**Evidence gap (not a code defect).** The last runtime proof run (13:48Z) predates the current verifier (13:54Z) and failed only because that intermediate probe read `expectedInkHeight` before writing it; its own snapshot shows all 128 members ready with finite visible bounds. The current, stricter probe — the live ink-height vs `fontHeight × fontSize/1000` proof that pins the actual-metrics requirement — has never executed, and narrow never ran in the harness-fix pass. Re-run `scripts/verify-handwriting-reference.mjs` (current revision) desktop+narrow to `verified` before closing G5; gates doc still shows pending, and this claims nothing about G6 or full-project acceptance.
